That's interesting, dual 1846S chips is something we have not seen before. Presumably one for UHF and one for VHF.  The MD2017 was one of the first dual band DMR radios so possibly they simply took two single band RF designs and put them on one PCB.  There is only one HRC6000 though so it can't be true dual receive on DMR.<br><br>I had always assumed that the  strange antenna shape was something to do with the GPS, but I see there is an internal GPS antenna and no obvious diplexing components on the external antenna input. <br><br>Colin G4EML<br><br>Q<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Mon Mar 06, 2023 10:27 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
